<title>POLAND: ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIPS POOL B RESULTS.</title>
<headline>ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIPS POOL B RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>KATOWICE, Poland 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of world</p>
<p>championship pool B ice hockey matches on Friday:</p>
<p>Switzerland 5  Belarus 6 (3-2 2-1 0-3)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Switzerland - Reto von Arx 3, Stefan Grogg 10, Franz Steffen</p>
<p>16, Andreas Naeser 24, Gian-Marco Crameri 37.</p>
<p>Belarus - Vadim Bekboulatov 1, 16, Andrei Skabelka 35, Oleg</p>
<p>Antonenko 43, Alexandre Andrievski 43, Andrei Kovalev 53.</p>
<p>Austria 2  Britain 2 (0-1 1-1 1-0)</p>
<p>Austria - Herbert Hohenberger 28, Martin Ulrich 55.</p>
<p>Britain - Kevin Conway 10, Douglas McEven 24</p>
<p>Kazakhstan 3  Poland 3 (3-0 0-1 0-2)</p>
<p>Kazakhstan - Vadim Glovatskiy 4, Maxim Komisarov 11, Yerlan</p>
<p>Sagymbayev 17.</p>
<p>Poland - Wojciech Tkacz 49, 59, Slawomir Wieloch 24</p>
<p>Denmark 4  Netherlands 6 (3-0 1-4 0-2)</p>
<p>Denmark - Jens Christian Jensen 10, 20, Soren Nielsen 1,</p>
<p>Ronny Struve Larsen 23.</p>
<p>Netherlands - David Livingston 31, 40, 59, Lester Arts 36,</p>
<p>Thomas Hartogs 38, Martinos Rison 45.</p>
<p>Pool B standings:</p>
<p>			 P    W    D    L    F    A    Pts</p>
<p> 1. Belarus	  5    5    0    0    36   15   10</p>
<p> 2. Kazakhstan     5    3    1    1    20   14    7</p>
<p> 3. Austria	  5    2    2    1    16   14    6</p>
<p> 4. Britain	  5    2    1    2    24   13    5</p>
<p> 5. Switzerland    5    2    1    2    21   17    5</p>
<p> 6. Poland	   5    1    2    2    13   19    4</p>
<p> 7. Netherlands    5    1    1    3    15   32    3</p>
<p> 8. Denmark	  5    0    0    5    13   33    0</p>
